# A walk through the whole approval chain, using the sample people.
#
# 1. In a terminal:  dotnet run --project src/PBRMS.Api
# 2. Needs the REST Client extension in VS Code. Click "Send Request" above each
#    block, IN ORDER FROM THE TOP: later steps use the answers from earlier ones.
#    The answer opens on the right.
#
# To go through it again, change @day to a date you haven't used. Or leave it the
# same to see a clash at step 7: the answer names the production in the way.

@api = http://localhost:5188
@day = 2026-12-01

### Is the API up, and can it reach the database?
GET {{api}}/health

### ---- Sign everyone in (Development only: no password) ----

### Producer
# @name producer
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "producer@pbrms.test" }

### Executive Producer
# @name ep
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ep@pbrms.test" }

### Camera supervisor
# @name supervisor
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@pbrms.test" }

### Booking Officer
# @name bookingOfficer
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "booking@pbrms.test" }

### Who am I? Shows the supervisor's roles.
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### Departments and divisions, sorted by name: Camera, News, Sound, Sports.
# @name units
GET {{api}}/org-units
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}

### ---- The approval chain ----

### 1. The producer fills in the booking form. Status: Draft.
# @name booking
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Morning Show",
  "departmentId": "{{units.response.body.$[1].id}}",
  "activityType": "Recording",
  "venue": "Studio1",
  "callAt": "{{day}}T06:00:00+02:00",
  "startsAt": "{{day}}T06:30:00+02:00",
  "endsAt": "{{day}}T09:00:00+02:00",
  "crewSlots": [
    { "divisionId": "{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}", "positionLabel": "Camera 1" }
  ]
}

### 2. The producer submits it. There is no Production Manager, so it goes straight to the EP. Status: EpReview.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Submit" }

### 3. It's in the Executive Producer's queue.
GET {{api}}/bookings/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{ep.response.body.token}}

### 4. The Executive Producer approves and sets the channel. It's a studio production, so "crewLead" is BookingOfficer. Anyone the roster has in Studio 1 is filled in automatically.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{ep.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Approve", "channel": "Nbc1" }

### 5. It's in the Booking Officer's queue. Supervisors don't see studio bookings.
GET {{api}}/bookings/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}

### 6. The Booking Officer opens the crew picker: Camera's operators.
# @name operators
GET {{api}}/org-units/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/operators
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}

### 7. The Booking Officer assigns the first operator. That fills the last position. Status: Finalisation. (If step 4 already filled it from the roster, this changes nothing.)
PUT {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/crew
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assignments": [
    { "slotId": "{{booking.response.body.$.crewSlots[0].id}}", "operatorId": "{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}" }
  ]
}

### 8. The Booking Officer checks for clashes. [] means none.
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/clashes
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}

### 9. The Booking Officer confirms. Status: Confirmed.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Approve" }

### 10. The finished booking: crew, and every step in "history".
GET {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}

### ---- Things that must be refused ----

### Approving a booking that is already confirmed. Answer: 409, with the reason.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Approve" }

### A form that ends before it starts. Answer: 400, with the reason.
POST {{api}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Backwards",
  "departmentId": "{{units.response.body.$[1].id}}",
  "activityType": "Recording",
  "venue": "Studio2",
  "callAt": "{{day}}T08:00:00+02:00",
  "startsAt": "{{day}}T10:00:00+02:00",
  "endsAt": "{{day}}T09:00:00+02:00"
}

### No token. Answer: 401.
GET {{api}}/me

### ---- Monthly roster (needs the sign-ins and "units" above, and step 6) ----
# Use a month with no bookings yet. Change @month to start a fresh roster.

@month = 2027-04

### The Camera legend: what each shift code means.
GET {{api}}/shift-definitions/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R1. The supervisor fills in two cells. Status: Draft.
PUT {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entries": [
    { "operatorId": "{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}", "date": "{{month}}-01", "code": "L" },
    { "operatorId": "{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}", "date": "{{month}}-02", "code": "A1" }
  ]
}

### R2. See the grid.
GET {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R3. Publish it. Status: Published. "clashes" lists any confirmed booking it upsets.
POST {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R4. Is that operator free on the 1st? No: they're on leave.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-01T09:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-01T11:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R5. On the 2nd, inside their 08h00–17h00 shift? Yes: [] means free.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-02T09:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-02T11:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### R6. In the evening of the 2nd? No: outside their shift.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-02T19:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-02T21:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### ---- Warnings and notifications (needs the sign-ins, "units" and step 6 above) ----
# Uses @month and the operator from the roster steps. Send R1 and R3 first.
# In that roster the operator is on leave on the 1st, and has an A1 shift on the 2nd.

### W1. A day off on the 3rd: add it to the roster...
PUT {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "entries": [{ "operatorId": "{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}", "date": "{{month}}-03", "code": "O" }] }

### W2. ...and publish it.
POST {{api}}/rosters/{{units.response.body.$[0].id}}/{{month}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### W3. The operator on leave on the 1st: "kind" is OnLeave, and it can't be overridden.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-01T09:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-01T11:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### W4. The operator on the 3rd: "kind" is CallIn and "isWarning" is true. To go ahead, send
# PUT /bookings/{id}/crew again with "acknowledgeWarnings": true. They are then notified.
GET {{api}}/operators/{{operators.response.body.$[0].id}}/conflicts?from={{month}}-03T09:00:00%2B02:00&to={{month}}-03T11:00:00%2B02:00
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.token}}

### W5. The producer's notifications, such as "is confirmed" from step 9.
GET {{api}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}

### W6. The producer marks the booking from step 1 as started.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "Start" }

### W7. ...and as ended. If it runs 30 minutes past its booked end before this, the
# supervisors are told automatically.
POST {{api}}/bookings/{{booking.response.body.id}}/transition
Authorization: Bearer {{producer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "End" }

### ---- Report for the TV Operations Manager ----

### Sign in as the TV Operations Manager
# @name manager
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "tvops.manager@pbrms.test" }

### Who was booked on a day off or outside their shift this month (@month from the roster steps).
GET {{api}}/reports/off-roster-work?from={{month}}-01&to={{month}}-28
Authorization: Bearer {{manager.response.body.token}}

### ---- Daily roster (uses @day from the top of the file) ----

### The sheet for the day: bookings, who is on duty, and what's still undecided.
GET {{api}}/daily-roster/{{day}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}

### The Booking Officer adds an announcement.
PUT {{api}}/daily-roster/{{day}}/announcement
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Fire drill at 10h00" }

### The Booking Officer adds a line of their own.
PUT {{api}}/daily-roster/{{day}}/lines
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "area": "Studio 3", "title": "Rig check", "startsAt": "{{day}}T08:00:00+02:00", "endsAt": "{{day}}T10:00:00+02:00" }

### The A4 printout. REST Client shows the file details; use "Save Response" to keep the PDF.
GET {{api}}/daily-roster/{{day}}/pdf
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}

### ---- APP bookings ----

### Sign in as an editor
# @name editor
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "editor@pbrms.test" }

### Sign in as the APP operator
# @name appOperator
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "app@pbrms.test" }

### The APP operators to choose from
# @name appOperators
GET {{api}}/app-operators
Authorization: Bearer {{editor.response.body.token}}

### When the APP room is taken, to pick a free time before booking.
GET {{api}}/app-room/busy?from={{day}}&to={{day}}
Authorization: Bearer {{editor.response.body.token}}

### A1. The editor books the APP operator directly. Status: Requested.
# @name session
POST {{api}}/app-sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{editor.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operatorId": "{{appOperators.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "production": "Evening News voice-over",
  "startsAt": "{{day}}T14:00:00+02:00",
  "endsAt": "{{day}}T15:30:00+02:00"
}

### A2. The APP operator confirms. Status: Confirmed. Or send A3 instead.
POST {{api}}/app-sessions/{{session.response.body.id}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{appOperator.response.body.token}}

### A3. Or they can't do that time, so it goes to the Booking Officer. Status: Unavailable.
POST {{api}}/app-sessions/{{session.response.body.id}}/unavailable
Authorization: Bearer {{appOperator.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "On a production at that time" }

### A4. The Booking Officer suggests a suitable time. Status: TimeSuggested.
POST {{api}}/app-sessions/{{session.response.body.id}}/suggest-time
Authorization: Bearer {{bookingOfficer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "{{day}}T16:00:00+02:00", "endsAt": "{{day}}T17:30:00+02:00" }

### A5. The editor accepts it. Status: Confirmed.
POST {{api}}/app-sessions/{{session.response.body.id}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{editor.response.body.token}}

### A6. Report: which productions, editors and producers used APP.
GET {{api}}/reports/app-usage?from={{day}}&to={{day}}
Authorization: Bearer {{manager.response.body.token}}
